Client construction & authentication — Two constructors — explicit credentials or load from `~/.vxcloud/credentials.json`. Auto-refresh JWT on 401 with single-flight semantics.
Explicit credentials:
```
import { VxCloud } from '@vxcloud/sdk';

const c = new VxCloud({
  apiKey:   'xc_live_…',
  username: 'your-username',
  // optional overrides:
  // vxcloudURL: 'https://api.vxcloud.io',
  // nodeURL:     'https://node1.vxcloud.io',
});

const me = await c.auth.whoami();
console.log(me.username);
```
Load from vxcli:
```
import { VxCloud } from '@vxcloud/sdk';

const c = await VxCloud.loadFromVxcli();
console.log(await c.auth.whoami());
```
Inject custom fetch (tests / Node <18):
```
import { VxCloud } from '@vxcloud/sdk';
import { fetch as undici } from 'undici';

const c = new VxCloud({
  apiKey: 'xc_test_…',
  username: 'tester',
  fetch: undici as unknown as typeof fetch,
});
```
Brand-name aliases (VxCloud / vxcloud / Vxsdk / Client):
```
// All four named exports below resolve to the SAME class. Pick the
// name your team prefers — there is no behavior difference.

import { VxCloud, vxcloud, Vxsdk, Client } from '@vxcloud/sdk';

console.log(VxCloud === vxcloud);   // true
console.log(VxCloud === Vxsdk);     // true
console.log(VxCloud === Client);    // true

// Any of these reads identically against the platform:
const c1 = await VxCloud.loadFromVxcli();
const c2 = await vxcloud.loadFromVxcli();
const c3 = await Vxsdk.loadFromVxcli();
const c4 = await Client.loadFromVxcli();

// Names match the Python SDK so the same snippet pattern works in both:
//   Python:     vxsdk.Client | vxsdk.VxCloud | vxsdk.vxcloud
//   TypeScript: { Client | VxCloud | vxcloud | Vxsdk } from '@vxcloud/sdk'
```

