cloud (vm / s3 / iam / network / database / kubernetes / serverless) — Per-provider helpers covering VM lifecycle, storage, IAM (policy / role / keypair), networking (VPC), managed databases, Kubernetes, and serverless. `c.cloud.vm.provision(...)` is the symmetric API shared with the Python SDK; pass `name` to use the prod-verified verbose body.
VM — provision / status / action (symmetric API):
```
// Pass `name` to use the prod-verified body shape (matches Python SDK).
const vm = await c.cloud.vm.provision({
  name: 'api-vm',
  cloud: 'aws', instanceType: 't3.small', region: 'us-east-1',
  keyPairName: 'AWSPRODKEY2',
  tags: { env: 'staging' },
});

// Lifecycle — start | stop | restart | reboot
const state = await c.cloud.vm.status({ instanceId: vm.instance_id as string, cloud: 'aws' });
await c.cloud.vm.action({ instanceId: vm.instance_id as string, action: 'restart', cloud: 'aws' });

// Flat shortcut that mirrors Python's `c.cloud.create_vm(...)`:
const vm2 = await c.cloud.createVm({
  name: 'worker-vm',
  cloud: 'aws', instanceType: 't3.small', region: 'us-east-1',
  keyPairName: 'AWSPRODKEY2',
});
```
S3 / IAM / keypair:
```
await c.cloud.s3.createBucket({ name: 'my-assets', region: 'us-east-1' });

await c.cloud.iam.createPolicy({
  name: 'read-only-s3',
  document: {
    Version: '2012-10-17',
    Statement: [{ Effect: 'Allow', Action: 's3:Get*', Resource: '*' }],
  },
});

await c.cloud.iam.createRole({
  name: 'svc-api-role',
  assumeRolePolicy: {
    Version: '2012-10-17',
    Statement: [{
      Effect: 'Allow',
      Principal: { Service: 'ec2.amazonaws.com' },
      Action: 'sts:AssumeRole',
    }],
  },
});

// Provision a keypair — private material lands in workspace Vault under `name`.
await c.cloud.iam.createKeypair({
  name: 'AWSPRODKEY3', region: 'us-east-1', cloud: 'aws',
});
