chunks.text:
agentcontrol (full /api/v2/agentcontrol/* surface — 22 sub-resources) — Full UI parity with /dashboard/?tab=agentcontrol. Original surfaces (fineTuning, training, knowledge, datasets, agents, github) plus the new sub-resources: embeddings, tools, mcp, evals, code, models, deployments, webAssets, benchmarks, catalog, health, events, llm, deployTargets, workflows, infra. Plus `runtimeMetrics(endpoint)` to proxy a marketplace agent's /metrics scrape through the node. `tenantId` is read from `~/.vxcloud/credentials.json` by `loadFromVxcli()` and sent as `X-Tenant-ID` on every request; pass `{ tenantId }` per call to override.
summary + list resources:
```
// Top-level dashboard summary — counts, recent activity, etc.
const summary = await c.agentcontrol.summary();
console.log(summary.totalModels, summary.activeTrainingJobs);

// Browse each surface
for (const j of await c.agentcontrol.fineTuning.list()) console.log('FT:',    j.id, j.status);
for (const t of await c.agentcontrol.training.list())   console.log('Train:', t.id, t.status);
for (const k of await c.agentcontrol.knowledge.list())  console.log('KB:',    k.id, k.name);
for (const d of await c.agentcontrol.datasets.list())   console.log('DS:',    d.id, d.rowCount);
```
Fine-tune a base model and wait for completion:
```
import type { LongRunningJob } from '@vxcloud/sdk';

// Start a fine-tuning job — returns a LongRunningJob handle.
const job: LongRunningJob = await c.agentcontrol.fineTuning.create({
  baseModel: 'claude-haiku-4-5',
  datasetId: 'ds-abc123',
  name:      'support-tone-v1',
  hyperparameters: { epochs: 3, learningRate: 1e-5 },
});

// Poll until terminal (succeeded | failed | cancelled | ready | error)
await job.waitForCompletion({
  timeoutMs: 60 * 60 * 1000,
  intervalMs: 10_000,
  onTick: (j) => console.log('progress:', j.progress, j.status),
});
console.log('final:', job.status, '· model:', job.data?.modelId);

// One-shot convenience that calls create + waitForCompletion:
//   const done = await c.agentcontrol.fineTuning.wait({ baseModel: ..., datasetId: ... });
```
vLLM serving artifact (deploy your model, OpenAI-compatible):
```
// Generate a deployable vLLM server (docker-compose + args + test curl)
// for a base model and optional LoRA adapters.
const art = await c.agentcontrol.vllmArtifact({
  model: 'mistralai/Mistral-7B-Instruct-v0.2',
  port: 8000, quantization: 'awq', maxModelLen: 8192,
  loraModules: [{ name: 'support', path: '/loras/support' }],  // optional
});
console.log(art.image);           // vllm/vllm-openai:latest
console.log(art.openai_base_url); // http://<host>:8000/v1
console.log(art.requires_gpu);    // true — deploy to a CUDA host
console.log(art.compose_yaml);    // docker-compose.yml to run the server
console.log(art.curl_example);    // POST /v1/chat/completions

// Then register the running .../v1 URL as a Model endpoint:
//   await c.agentcontrol.deployments.create({ name: 'mistral-vllm', modelId: '...' });
```
Datasets — preview + upload:
```
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';

// Inspect dataset contents before training
