salesshift + leads (tracked email and the prospect pool) — Two namespaces, deliberately kept apart: `c.salesshift` is the send surface, `c.leads` is the pool — because a lead is not mailable until it becomes a Contact. 22 methods covering 20 of SalesShift’s 306 routes and none of its 57 messaging routes; deals, sequences, quotes, contracts, invoices, calendar and deliverability have no SDK method in any language. This is the most thoroughly typed of the five bindings — ~30 exported interfaces and unions, overloads that make `searchLeads({resultType:'company'})` return a company page, the server caps exported as constants, and named errors. Status: read in full, but not built or executed in the pass that produced this page — `getStats()` is also the one call with no result interface (it returns `Record<string, unknown>`).
Tracked email + worker health:
```
import { VxCloud } from '@vxcloud/sdk';

const c = await VxCloud.loadFromVxcli();

const stats = await c.salesshift.getStats();   // Record<string, unknown>

for (const m of await c.salesshift.listEmails('sent')) {
  console.log(m.toEmail, m.status, m.openCount);
}

const sent = await c.salesshift.sendEmail({
  toEmail:  'ada@acme.com',
  subject:  'Following up, {{first_name}}',
  bodyHtml: '<p>Saw you shipped v2 — worth 15 minutes?</p>',
});
console.log(sent.trackingId, sent.provider);
// provider ∈ node-smtp | smtp | sendgrid | mailgun | platform | sink

// The email worker lives on your tenant node, not the control plane.
const health = await c.salesshift.getWorkerHealth();
console.log(health.status, health.providers, health.redisConnected);
```
Search — typed filters and an overload for companies:
```
$27
```
Caps and named errors:
```
import {
  LEADS_MAX_BATCH,        // 200  — save / convertFromPool
  LEADS_MAX_PAGE_SIZE,    // 100  — searchLeads limit
  LEADS_MAX_LIST_LIMIT,   // 500  — listLeads limit
  LEADS_TOTAL_CAP,        // 10000 — display cap on a match count
  VxLeadQuotaExceededError,
  VxLeadErasedError,
} from '@vxcloud/sdk';

// The caps are exported so you can chunk BEFORE a round trip fails.
for (let i = 0; i < poolIds.length; i += LEADS_MAX_BATCH) {
  await c.leads.saveLeads(poolIds.slice(i, i + LEADS_MAX_BATCH));
}

try {
  await c.leads.revealLead(poolId);
} catch (e) {
  if (e instanceof VxLeadQuotaExceededError) {
    // 402 — allowance spent. NOTHING was charged for this attempt.
  } else if (e instanceof VxLeadErasedError) {
    // 410 — removed at the person's request, for every tenant. Terminal.
  } else {
    throw e;
  }
}
```
Reveal → convert → send:
```
$28
```
Saved leads, searches, enrich, erasure:
```
