Production notes & known issues — Real failure modes you will hit at least once. Same content as the CLI "Operational gotchas" section, adapted to SDK usage.
Keypair MUST be in Vault for stack deploys:
```
// c.deploy.fastapi / react / nextjs / ... server-side validates
// 'key_pair_name' as required and ignores private_key_pem entirely.
// Upload the key to Vault once:
//
//   vxcli configure setup vm --key-pair-name MYKEY --pem-file ./mykey.pem
//
// c.deploy.container() DOES accept a local PEM via privateKeyPem.
```
command is comma-split server-side:
```
// The container deploy endpoint splits 'command' on commas and strips
// quotes before docker run. Inline structured config (JSON / YAML)
// gets destroyed. Only safe for comma-free single tokens.
//
// BAD (mangled):
//   command: '--config=yaml:{"receivers":{...}}'
// GOOD: stage the config on the VM, then mount + reference it:

await c.deploy.container({
  image:   'otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib:latest',
  volumes: ['/opt/otelcol-config.yaml:/etc/otelcol-contrib/config.yaml'],
  command: '--config=/etc/otelcol-contrib/config.yaml',     // no commas
  ports:   ['13133:13133', '4318:4318'],
  enableSsl: true, domain: 'otel.example.com', sslEmail: 'ops@example.com',
  host: 'h', sshUser: 'u', keyPairName: 'k',
});
```
TCP services 502 on the HTTPS endpoint:
```
// --enable-ssl puts an HTTP nginx proxy in front of --port. Nginx HTTP
// cannot speak postgres / redis / etc. wire protocols → https://<domain>
// returns 502. The deploy itself is fine; connect on the raw TCP port.
await c.deploy.container({
  image: 'postgres:16', name: 'postgres',
  env:   ['POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme'],
  ports: ['5432:5432'],
  enableSsl: true, domain: 'db.example.com', sslEmail: 'ops@example.com',
  host: 'h', sshUser: 'u', keyPairName: 'k',
});
// psql -h db.example.com -p 5432 -U postgres  -> works
// curl https://db.example.com/                -> 502 — expected
```
Cloudflare HTTP 524 on slow deploys ≠ failure:
```
import { VxServerError } from '@vxcloud/sdk';

try {
  await c.deploy.container({ image: 'sebp/elk', ports: ['5601:5601'], /* … */ });
} catch (err) {
  if (err instanceof VxServerError && /524/.test(String(err))) {
    // node1 is fronted by Cloudflare (~120s proxy-read timeout).
    // The deploy keeps running on the node — poll docker ps or
    // c.sessions.list({ status: 'running' }) instead of retrying.
  } else { throw err; }
}
```

