nodes (list / register self-hosted / update / delete) — Tenant-node CRUD against the VxCloud control plane. The Go SDK mirrors `vxcli node {list,add,update,delete,set-default}` 1:1. Self-hosted (BYO) registration uses POST /api/v1/auth/nodes/self-hosted, partial updates go through PATCH /api/v1/auth/nodes/{id}, deletes via DELETE /api/v1/auth/nodes/{id}.
List / default / set-default:
```
import "github.com/prodxcloud/vxcloud/nodes"

all, _ := c.Nodes().List(ctx)
for _, n := range all {
    fmt.Println(n.ID, n.Label(), n.BaseURL(),
        map[bool]string{true: "DEFAULT", false: ""}[n.IsDefaultNode])
}

def, _ := c.Nodes().Default(ctx)
fmt.Println("default node:", def.Label())

_ = c.Nodes().SetDefault(ctx, def.ID)
```
Register a self-hosted vxnode (BYO hardware):
```
node, err := c.Nodes().RegisterSelfHosted(ctx, nodes.RegisterSelfHostedInput{
    Hostname:         "prod-east-1",
    CustomDomainName: "prod.example.com",   // scheme stripped automatically
    Port:             8744,
    TunnelProvider:   "cloudflare",          // cloudflare | tailscale | caddy | direct
    KeyPairName:      "AWSPRODKEY1",
    Description:      "Prod fleet, us-east",
})
if err != nil { panic(err) }
fmt.Println("registered id=", node.ID)

// Promote it to default
_ = c.Nodes().SetDefault(ctx, node.ID)
```
Update (partial) — pointer fields distinguish unset from empty:
```
// Only non-nil fields are sent. Backend rejects read-only fields
// (public_ip, instance_id, ram_gb, cpu_cores).
host := "prod-east-1-renamed"
status := "stopped"
storage := "nvme"
backup := "daily"
addr := "s3://backups/n71/"

updated, err := c.Nodes().Update(ctx, 71, nodes.UpdateInput{
    Hostname:             &host,
    Status:               &status,
    StorageType:          &storage,
    StorageBackupMode:    &backup,
    StorageBackupAddress: &addr,
})
if err != nil { panic(err) }
fmt.Println("updated:", updated.Label(), updated.Status)
```
Delete a node record:
```
// Only deletes the row — terminate any underlying VM separately
// via your cloud provider. Self-hosted (BYO) nodes are fully removed
// since there's no VM to clean up.
if err := c.Nodes().Delete(ctx, 71); err != nil {
    panic(err)
}
```

