Production notes & known issues — Real failure modes you will hit at least once. Same content as the CLI "Operational gotchas" section, adapted to SDK usage.
Keypair MUST be in Vault for stack deploys:
```
// c.Deploy().Stack("fastapi"/"react"/"nextjs"/...) server-side
// validates KeyPairName as required and ignores any PEM. Upload once:
//
//   vxcli configure setup vm --key-pair-name MYKEY --pem-file ./mykey.pem
//
// c.Deploy().Container() accepts deploy.SSH{...KeyPairName...} from Vault
// OR a local PEM via deploy.SSH{...PrivateKeyPEM: ...}.
```
Command is comma-split server-side:
```
// The container deploy endpoint splits Command on every comma and
// strips quotes before docker run. Inline structured config will be
// destroyed. Only safe for comma-free single tokens.
//
// BAD (mangled):
//   Command: `--config=yaml:{"receivers":{...}}`
// GOOD: stage the config on the VM, then mount + reference:

c.Deploy().Container(ctx, deploy.ContainerOpts{
    SSH:     install.SSH{Host: "h", User: "u", KeyPairName: "k"},
    Image:   "otel/opentelemetry-collector-contrib:latest",
    Volumes: []string{"/opt/otelcol-config.yaml:/etc/otelcol-contrib/config.yaml"},
    Command: "--config=/etc/otelcol-contrib/config.yaml",   // no commas
    Ports:   []string{"13133:13133", "4318:4318"},
    EnableSSL: true, Domain: "otel.example.com", SSLEmail: "ops@example.com",
})
```
TCP services 502 on the HTTPS endpoint:
```
// --enable-ssl puts an HTTP nginx proxy in front of the first port.
// Nginx HTTP cannot speak postgres/redis/etc. wire protocols, so
// https://<domain> returns 502. The deploy itself is fine.
c.Deploy().Container(ctx, deploy.ContainerOpts{
    SSH:   install.SSH{Host: "h", User: "u", KeyPairName: "k"},
    Image: "postgres:16",
    Env:   []string{"POSTGRES_PASSWORD=changeme"},
    Ports: []string{"5432:5432"},
    EnableSSL: true, Domain: "db.example.com", SSLEmail: "ops@example.com",
})
// psql -h db.example.com -p 5432 -U postgres   -> works
// curl https://db.example.com/                 -> 502 — expected
```
Cloudflare HTTP 524 on slow deploys ≠ failure:
```
import vxerrors "github.com/prodxcloud/vxcloud/errors"

_, err := c.Deploy().Container(ctx, deploy.ContainerOpts{
    Image: "sebp/elk", Ports: []string{"5601:5601"},
    /* … */
})
if err != nil {
    var serr *vxerrors.ServerError
    if errors.As(err, &serr) && strings.Contains(err.Error(), "524") {
        // node1 is fronted by Cloudflare (~120s proxy-read timeout).
        // The deploy keeps running on the node — poll docker ps / sessions
        // rather than retrying (retrying duplicates the job).
        return
    }
    panic(err)
}
```

