- invited_as versus signed_as is deliberate: it records that the person invited as one name typed another, rather than quietly overwriting the invitation.
- content_sha256 is captured at each signature and again at completion. It is the hash of the document text that was signed, which is what makes a later “that is not what I agreed to” answerable.
